@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+<?php
+/**
+ * Tab Title: Call Bridge
+ * Tab Order: 40
+ */
+defined('ABSPATH') || exit;
+if(!current_user_can('manage_options'))return;
+?>
+<h2>Call Bridge operations guide</h2>
+<p>Call Bridge handles Twilio calls, dynamic number insertion (DNI), exclusive leases, attribution and internal duration/outcome qualification. Configuration completeness never proves calling acceptance.</p>
+<p><a href="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url('admin.php?page=secb-settings')); ?>">Setup &amp; Status</a> · <a href="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url('admin.php?page=secb-numbers')); ?>">Tracking Numbers</a> · <a href="<?php echo esc_url(admin_url('admin.php?page=secb-calls')); ?>">Call Log</a></p>
+<h3>Prerequisites and secure provisioning</h3>
+<p>Use WordPress 6.4+, PHP 8.1+, database access and required extensions including mysqli, mbstring, JSON, hash and OpenSSL. Verify web PHP separately from CLI PHP. Base is optional: it supplies shared facts/navigation and this tab; CB retains standalone pages without it. Webhooks need reachable HTTPS, correct proxy reconstruction and an owned Voice-capable Twilio number.</p>
+<p>Have the administrator preserve the existing external configuration outside the web root and replaceable plugin directory. Define <code>SECB_CONFIG_FILE</code> before plugin loading and use secret-file permissions readable by the actual web owner. Never copy another site's secrets or place them in wp_options, JavaScript, Git, tickets or screenshots. This UI neither edits nor displays credentials.</p>
+<p>Account SID identifies the account. Auth Token authenticates incoming signatures. Optional API Key SID/Secret is preferred for media retrieval; Account SID/Auth Token is the playback fallback. API keys cannot replace the webhook Auth Token. Leave optional media credentials absent while recording is off. Nonempty placeholders are not valid configuration; presence checks do not validate credentials or contact Twilio.</p>
+<h3>Public phone, forwarding destination and tracking number</h3>
+<p>The public business phone is the ordinary advertised contact. Each CB row's <code>forward_to</code> is the recipient destination. A tracking number is an owned Twilio number temporarily displayed to an attributed visitor. These three roles are not interchangeable. Base's legacy Forwarding / Tracking Phone field is an unconfirmed reference, not routing authority. No automatic synchronization occurs.</p>
+<p>Choose dedicated numbers and approved recipients before registration. Obtain/purchase numbers in Twilio only with separate operator authorization. A CB row neither purchases numbers nor updates provider webhooks. Preserve source/pool, forwarding, thresholds, active flags, recording flags, notices and whispers. Do not repoint a live client's number for diagnostics.</p>
+<h3>Twilio webhooks and staged verification</h3>
+<p>Use the exact site-derived URLs on Setup &amp; Status. Inbound Voice uses POST. CB generates the POST Dial status action, optional POST recording callback and signed GET whisper query in TwiML. Do not substitute health for Voice or manually configure a static whisper message URL.</p>
+<p>After approved provider setup, test signatures against the exact public URL, URI/query and form body. <code>SECB_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL</code> must agree with what Twilio signs through the proxy. Verify HTTPS/certificate trust, redirects, subdirectory sites and public connectivity. Do not disable validation to obtain a pass. Signed fixtures and a real authorized call are separate evidence.</p>
+<h3>DNI eligibility and attribution</h3>
+<p>DNI starts when supported click/UTM attribution or stored context exists. Capture includes GCLID, GBRAID, WBRAID, FBCLID, MSCLKID and UTM fields. Browser context uses <code>secb_attribution</code> in localStorage. Test unavailable/malformed storage and network failure. A mutable session is not an immutable attribution history.</p>
+<p>Ordinary tel links swap only when their original number matches an active tracking row's forwarding destination. Explicit opt-ins are <code>[data-se-phone]</code>, <code>[data-se-call-tracking]</code> and <code>.se-tracking-number</code>. Unrelated numbers and non-phone labels must remain unchanged. Test actual blocks/theme, late-added nodes and navigation. Do not change the site's global contact phone to test DNI.</p>
+<h3>Exclusive leases, pool sizing and exhaustion</h3>
+<p>Lease defaults to 30 minutes (5–240); attribution retention defaults to 90 days (1–365). Long attribution retention is not a long exclusive lease. The browser renews near half the lease duration; failed renewal restores original contact details rather than trusting a cached tracking number.</p>
+<p>For a source, CB selects the largest configured pool group. Ungrouped numbers each form a standalone one-number group; standalone numbers are not silently merged. Size that chosen pool for simultaneous attributed visitors throughout the lease window. Test independent database connections and browsers. Exhaustion fails closed: no shared busy number or guessed attribution, and ordinary contact details stay visible. Configuration checks do not prove concurrency safety.</p>
+<h3>Whispers, repeat callers and duration qualification</h3>
+<p>New/repeat whispers are recipient messages before bridging, not CRM campaigns. Repeat detection considers prior completed calls meeting the minimum duration within the row's repeat window. Repeat is metadata: returning callers are not suppressed for life or automatically marked Won/Lost.</p>
+<p>Completed calls meeting the duration threshold are internally qualified; short completed calls and other outcomes differ. Duration qualification does not prove business qualification, consent or a won job. Test threshold edges, busy/no-answer, retries, reordered callbacks and parent/child-leg correlation. Canonical identity remains <code>twilio:{CallSid}</code>.</p>
+<h3>Recording defaults, approved notices and secured playback</h3>
+<p>Recording defaults off per number. Enabling it requires approved notice language, participants/policy and separate authorization. When enabled, the notice precedes dual-channel recording from answer. Passthrough bypasses normal attribution/logging but does not turn recording off; it is not a no-recording diagnostic switch.</p>
+<p>Playback is intended for logged-in administrators with manage_options, using server-side credentials. Actual browser cookie/REST nonce behavior, the Call Log Play link, denied access, upstream URL/redirect trust and caching require separate acceptance. Never expose authorization headers or stored recording URLs, retrieve existing media as fixtures, or weaken access controls to get playback working. This guide fetches no media.</p>
+<h3>Diagnostics and interpreting status</h3>
+<p>Configuration needed means required information or a local prerequisite is missing. Off is valid for optional recording/debug features. Configuration complete is only a local presence check: live calling, attribution and playback remain pending. Number ownership, credential validity, valid signatures and delivery cannot be inferred from a configured row or badge.</p>
+<p>CLI commands include <code>wp se-call doctor</code>, <code>wp se-call webhook-status</code> and targeted <code>wp se-call inspect-call</code>. inspect-call still exposes operational fields; do not share raw output. Latest-event timestamps are not a durable retry journal. Health's <code>ok:true</code> is not acceptance; inspect individual fields and share only redacted evidence.</p>
+<p>WordPress bootstrap may create/update tables, save the DB version and schedule missing GC. Nominal doctor/health probes can inherit those writes. GET <code>/track/number</code> expires leases; session/callback requests also write state. Obtain appropriate authorization. The Setup &amp; Status and Help renderers themselves do not perform those operations.</p>
+<h3>Caching, proxy and failure troubleshooting</h3>
+<p>For absent swaps, check attribution eligibility, source/selected pool, active numbers, forward-number matching, storage and network failures. Check page-cache/minification behavior and late DOM content. Preserve unrelated tel links and verify safe restoration under exhaustion.</p>
+<p>For signature failures, compare approved public base, method, URI/query and form parameters through the actual proxy. Never print tokens or signature headers. For forwarding issues, verify the owned number and approved row destination. Fail-safe can preserve a resolved destination after some tracking/logging errors; it cannot guarantee delivery before number resolution. Never break a shared database as a test.</p>
+<h3>Maintenance, retention, upgrades and uninstall</h3>
+<p>Hourly <code>se_cb_gc</code> expires stale active leases and purges expired attribution sessions, not calls or recordings. Define their retention separately. Deactivation clears CB's GC hook. Activation/ordinary boot may install/upgrade tables and schedule GC. Check physical schema as well as the saved version after authorized upgrades.</p>
+<p>Preserve packages, external config, per-number settings and useful data before upgrades; test in isolation. Uninstall preserves CB tables by default. <code>SECB_ALLOW_UNINSTALL_DROP=true</code> explicitly permits destructive removal; never enable it for routine upgrades/diagnostics. Roll back only assigned files/fixtures, not unrelated plugins, cron hooks or the whole database.</p>
+<h3>Acceptance checklist and current limits</h3>
+<p>Record distinct evidence for package/configuration, SQL lease concurrency, browser DNI, valid/invalid signed callbacks, approved live forwarding/whispers/outcomes and secured playback. Use dedicated approved numbers/recipients. A skipped stage stays pending; this UI cannot mark calling accepted.</p>
+<p>No authoritative browser consent linkage exists: receipt columns and voice-copy logic do not establish browser → receipt → call authority. There is no CRM inquiry integration, call export, SMS workflow or provider picker. Twilio is the only provider. Consent/CRM/advertising interfaces need separate reviewed contracts. Configuration and duration checks do not establish legal or advertising compliance.</p>
